  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Closing the Accountability Gap to Better Protect Victims/Survivors of Sexual Exploitation, Abuse and Harassment (SEAH) in  de Aid Sector 2.0</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Closing the Accountability Gap to Better Protect Victims/Survivors of Sexual Exploitation, Abuse and Harassment (SEAH) in  de Aid Sector 2.0 To give a voice to SEAH victims/survivors and support the design of accountability mechanisms that work for them. Developing an accountability system that aligns with the Core Humanitarian Standard and: &#x2022; Caters to victims/survivors needs and respect their wishes &#x2022; Is appropriate, relevant, acceptable, designed and used by the community &#x2022; Facilitates reporting of SEAH complaints by overcoming barriers &#x2022; Investigates complaints promptly, confidentially, and thoroughly in a victim/survivor-centred way &#x2022; Holds perpetrators to account &#x2022; Provides redress for the victim/survivor Key Objectives: 1:  to define PSEAH process from SEAH violation to redress, mechanisms used, barriers and actors involved. 2: to conduct country specific community research into PSEAH in 3 distinct humanitarian settings 3:  to pilot solutions with local stakeholders in the 3 settings. 4. to identify and share lessons learnt from the 3 countries to develop scalable and replicable PSEAH solutions at global level.</narrative>
  </description>
